Confusing and contradictory


07 Jan 2021 15:58






Skips are supposed to use metric measurements; if imperial units are included at all, they should follow the metric units in parentheses. For instance: 2 meters (78 inches) long.
Is this skip known to harm itself? 
Does it hate all other lifeforms and attempt instant kills, or does it behave affectionately to a few exceptions who can handle it safely?
What biological features imply that #5334 evolved to live on a high-gravity gas giant, not a terrestrial planet? Gazing at Jupiter for no apparent reason seems bizarre.









 not all surreal strangeness HAS to be evil, deadly, or even scary.






